  "description": "Impressive 4th floor two bedroom apartment with direct west facing waterfront views onto the River Liffey, the Canal and the Samuel Beckett Bridge. 39 Hill of Down is located within a much sought after award winning development in the heart of the Docklands.\n\nBright and spacious throughout, this apartment features two large balconies, double height ceilings; energy efficient heating system; on-site concierge service; tranquil central courtyards with water features and floor to ceiling glazing. Accommodation extends to 95 sq. m. and comprises entrance hallway with storage closet, open plan living/dining and kitchen all finished to an excellent standard, two double bedrooms, master en-suite (with a separate shower and bath) and a further bathroom.\n\n\nLocation\nLocated in the heart of Dublin Docklands and with its own Luas stop, this central location is one of Dublin's most sought after addresses. Convenient to a range of landmarks including the Dublin Convention Centre, IFSC, City Centre, Grand Canal Dock, and the Three Arena. Spencer Dock is a luxury development in the heart of Dublin's financial district with a range of bars, cafés restaurants, and amenities on the doorstep. The Samuel Beckett Bridge allows a five minute walk to Grand Canal Dock and all the amenities it has to offer.\n\n\nFeatures\nStunning views from the living room and private balcony\nContemporary apartment with high ceilings\nSpacious 4th floor two bedroom apartment with a car space\nFully equipped kitchen with integrated appliances\nLocated at the Spencer Dock Luas Stop\nOn-site concierge service\nCar parking optional at an additional €100.00 per month",
